IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc3-proceedings.l4 -- Criminal Code (Canada), PART II.1 Terrorism, "Proceedings and Aggravated Punishment": sections 83.24 to 83.29.
-- Layer 1 (the law, objectively), written by part agent ccc3 from the text alone. The text is a plain-text rendering of the Justice Laws Website
-- consolidation (current to 2026-09-30); it is not the official text. Sections 83.28 and 83.29 are shown repealed.
--
-- READING A RESULT (rule of 2026-10-29 and the ruling of 2026-11-12): as in `ccc3-interpretation.l4`. A prohibition limited by its own wording ("without the consent", "any of sections ...")
-- answers NOTHING outside the limit; a power with an "if" gate answers NOTHING when the gate fails (tag GATE-A); a "may" function gated by "Where" answers JUST FALSE as the 2026-11-05 rulings say and is listed
-- for a lawyer (tag GATE-B); "other than X" is a flat exclusion answered JUST FALSE (a case-by-case site: fork F-ccc3-9). A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- Section numbers are decimals, so "83.02 to 83.04 and 83.18 to 83.23" takes in 83.181, 83.19, 83.191, 83.2, 83.201, 83.202, 83.21, 83.22, 83.221, 83.222, 83.223 and 83.23, and NOT 83.231 (the hoax offence), which is greater than 83.23.

§ `Section 83.24 -- Attorney General's consent`

-- "Proceedings in respect of a terrorism offence or an offence under section 83.12 shall not be commenced without the consent of the Attorney General": a bar limited by its own wording to those offences and to the absence of consent.
-- COVERS: fork F-ccc3-16 | s 83.24 the proceedings are barred from being commenced | s 83.24
-- src:1777 | Proceedings and Aggravated Punishment
-- src:1778 | Attorney General’s consent
-- src:1779 | 83.24 Proceedings in respect of a terrorism offence or an offence under section 83.12 shall not be commenced without the consent of the Attorney General.
@ref s 83.24 (src:1777-1779)
GIVEN `the offence is a terrorism offence, by s 2 terrorism offence` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the offence is an offence under section 83.12` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Attorney General has consented` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.24 the proceedings are barred from being commenced` MEANS
    IF `the Attorney General has consented`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "shall not be commenced without the consent of the Attorney General"
    ELSE IF `the offence is an offence under section 83.12`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE CONSIDER `the offence is a terrorism offence, by s 2 terrorism offence`
              WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
              WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Proceedings in respect of a terrorism offence or an offence under section 83.12"
              WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the offence is a terrorism offence is for s 2

§ `Section 83.25 -- Jurisdiction`

-- (1) "Where a person is alleged to have committed a terrorism offence or an offence under section 83.12, proceedings ... may, whether or not that person is in Canada, be commenced at the instance of the Government of Canada and conducted by the Attorney General of Canada
-- or counsel acting on his or her behalf in any territorial division in Canada, if the offence is alleged to have occurred outside the province in which the proceedings are commenced, whether or not proceedings have previously been commenced elsewhere in Canada."
-- GATE-B: "Where"; GATE-A: "if the offence is alleged to have occurred outside the province". Whether the person is in Canada, and whether proceedings were begun elsewhere, do not matter.
-- COVERS: fork F-ccc3-11,F-ccc3-20 | s 83.25(1) the proceedings may be commenced at the instance of the Government of Canada | s 83.25(1)
-- src:1780 | Jurisdiction
-- src:1781 | 83.25 (1) Where a person is alleged to have committed a terrorism offence or an offence under section 83.12, proceedings in respect of that offence may, whether or not that person is in Canada, be commenced at the instance of the Government of Canada and conducted by the Attorney General of Canada or counsel acting on his or her behalf in any territorial division in Canada, if the offence is alleged to have occurred outside the province in which the proceedings are commenced, whether or not proceedings have previously been commenced elsewhere in Canada.
@ref s 83.25(1) (src:1780-1781)
GIVEN `the person is alleged to have committed a terrorism offence, by s 2 terrorism offence` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is alleged to have committed an offence under section 83.12` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offence is alleged to have occurred outside the province in which the proceedings are commenced` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.25(1) the proceedings may be commenced at the instance of the Government of Canada` MEANS
    IF `the person is alleged to have committed an offence under section 83.12`
    THEN `the answer on the place`
    ELSE CONSIDER `the person is alleged to have committed a terrorism offence, by s 2 terrorism offence`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN `the answer on the place`
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a person is alleged to have committed a terrorism offence or an offence under section 83.12"
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the offence is a terrorism offence is for s 2
    WHERE
        `the answer on the place` MEANS
            IF `the offence is alleged to have occurred outside the province in which the proceedings are commenced`
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the offence is alleged to have occurred outside the province in which the proceedings are commenced"

-- COVERS: encoded | s 83.25(2) the accused may be tried and punished as if the offence had been committed in the territorial division | s 83.25(2)
-- src:1782 | Trial and punishment
-- src:1783 | (2) An accused may be tried and punished in respect of an offence referred to in subsection (1) in the same manner as if the offence had been committed in the territorial division where the proceeding is conducted.
@ref s 83.25(2) (src:1782-1783)
GIVEN `it is an offence referred to in subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.25(2) the accused may be tried and punished as if the offence had been committed in the territorial division` MEANS
    IF `it is an offence referred to in subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An accused may be tried and punished in respect of an offence referred to in subsection (1)"

§ `Section 83.26 -- Sentences to be served consecutively`

-- "A sentence, other than one of life imprisonment, imposed on a person for an offence under any of sections 83.02 to 83.04 and 83.18 to 83.23 shall be served consecutively to (a) any other punishment imposed on the person, other than a sentence of life imprisonment,
-- for an offence arising out of the same event or series of events; and (b) any other sentence, other than one of life imprisonment, to which the person is subject at the time the sentence is imposed on the person for an offence under any of those sections."
-- "any of sections 83.02 to 83.04 and 83.18 to 83.23" is a scope limit with no "only": outside it, NOTHING (ruling (c) of 2026-11-05); "other than one of life imprisonment" is a flat exclusion: JUST FALSE.
-- COVERS: fork F-ccc3-9 | s 83.26(a) the sentence is to be served consecutively to the other punishment; s 83.26(b) the sentence is to be served consecutively to the other sentence | s 83.26*
-- src:1784 | Sentences to be served consecutively
-- src:1785 | 83.26 A sentence, other than one of life imprisonment, imposed on a person for an offence under any of sections 83.02 to 83.04 and 83.18 to 83.23 shall be served consecutively to
-- src:1786 | (a) any other punishment imposed on the person, other than a sentence of life imprisonment, for an offence arising out of the same event or series of events; and
-- src:1787 | (b) any other sentence, other than one of life imprisonment, to which the person is subject at the time the sentence is imposed on the person for an offence under any of those sections.
@ref s 83.26 (src:1784-1787)
GIVEN `the offence the sentence is imposed for` IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `the sentence is one of life imprisonment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other punishment is a sentence of life imprisonment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other punishment is for an offence arising out of the same event or series of events` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.26(a) the sentence is to be served consecutively to the other punishment` MEANS
    IF NOT `the offence the sentence is imposed for is within sections 83.02 to 83.04 and 83.18 to 83.23`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for an offence under any of sections 83.02 to 83.04 and 83.18 to 83.23"
    ELSE IF `the sentence is one of life imprisonment`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A sentence, other than one of life imprisonment"
         ELSE IF `the other punishment is a sentence of life imprisonment`
              THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "any other punishment imposed on the person, other than a sentence of life imprisonment"
              ELSE IF `the other punishment is for an offence arising out of the same event or series of events`
                   THEN JUST TRUE
                   ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for an offence arising out of the same event or series of events"
    WHERE
        `the offence the sentence is imposed for is within sections 83.02 to 83.04 and 83.18 to 83.23` MEANS
            (`the offence the sentence is imposed for`'s `section` AT LEAST 83.02 AND `the offence the sentence is imposed for`'s `section` AT MOST 83.04)
            OR (`the offence the sentence is imposed for`'s `section` AT LEAST 83.18 AND `the offence the sentence is imposed for`'s `section` AT MOST 83.23)

@ref s 83.26 (src:1784-1787)
GIVEN `the offence the sentence is imposed for` IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `the sentence is one of life imprisonment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other sentence is one of life imprisonment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is subject to the other sentence when this sentence is imposed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other sentence is for an offence under any of those sections` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.26(b) the sentence is to be served consecutively to the other sentence` MEANS
    IF NOT `the offence the sentence is imposed for is within sections 83.02 to 83.04 and 83.18 to 83.23`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for an offence under any of sections 83.02 to 83.04 and 83.18 to 83.23"
    ELSE IF `the sentence is one of life imprisonment`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A sentence, other than one of life imprisonment"
         ELSE IF `the other sentence is one of life imprisonment`
              THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "any other sentence, other than one of life imprisonment"
              ELSE IF `the person is subject to the other sentence when this sentence is imposed` AND `the other sentence is for an offence under any of those sections`
                   THEN JUST TRUE
                   ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to which the person is subject at the time the sentence is imposed on the person for an offence under any of those sections"
    WHERE
        `the offence the sentence is imposed for is within sections 83.02 to 83.04 and 83.18 to 83.23` MEANS
            (`the offence the sentence is imposed for`'s `section` AT LEAST 83.02 AND `the offence the sentence is imposed for`'s `section` AT MOST 83.04)
            OR (`the offence the sentence is imposed for`'s `section` AT LEAST 83.18 AND `the offence the sentence is imposed for`'s `section` AT MOST 83.23)

§ `Section 83.27 -- Punishment for terrorist activity`

-- (1) "Notwithstanding anything in this Act, a person convicted of an indictable offence, other than an offence for which a sentence of imprisonment for life is imposed as a minimum punishment, where the act or omission constituting the offence also constitutes a terrorist activity, is liable to imprisonment for life."
-- "other than ..." is a flat exclusion (JUST FALSE); "where the act or omission ... also constitutes a terrorist activity" is a "where" condition (JUST FALSE when it fails).
-- COVERS: fork F-ccc3-9 | s 83.27(1) the person is liable to imprisonment for life; s 83.27(1) the punishment the person is liable to | s 83.27(1)
-- src:1788 | Punishment for terrorist activity
-- src:1789 | 83.27 (1) Notwithstanding anything in this Act, a person convicted of an indictable offence, other than an offence for which a sentence of imprisonment for life is imposed as a minimum punishment, where the act or omission constituting the offence also constitutes a terrorist activity, is liable to imprisonment for life.
@ref s 83.27(1) (src:1788-1789)
GIVEN `the person is convicted of an indictable offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a sentence of imprisonment for life is imposed for the offence as a minimum punishment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act or omission constituting the offence also constitutes a terrorist activity, by s 83.01(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.27(1) the person is liable to imprisonment for life` MEANS
    IF NOT `the person is convicted of an indictable offence`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a person convicted of an indictable offence"
    ELSE IF `a sentence of imprisonment for life is imposed for the offence as a minimum punishment`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "other than an offence for which a sentence of imprisonment for life is imposed as a minimum punishment"
         ELSE CONSIDER `the act or omission constituting the offence also constitutes a terrorist activity, by s 83.01(1)`
              WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
              WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the act or omission constituting the offence also constitutes a terrorist activity"
              WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the act is a terrorist activity is for s 83.01(1)

@ref s 83.27(1) (src:1788-1789)
`s 83.27(1) the punishment the person is liable to` MEANS
    Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for life`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

-- (2) "Subsection (1) does not apply unless the prosecutor satisfies the court that the offender, before making a plea, was notified that the application of that subsection would be sought."
-- JUST TRUE: subsection (1) does not apply (no such notice proved); NOTHING once the "unless" is met (the subsection then says nothing more: fork F-ccc3-5).
-- COVERS: fork F-ccc3-5 | s 83.27(2) subsection (1) does not apply; s 83.27 the person is liable to imprisonment for life, subject to subsection (2) | s 83.27(2)
-- src:1790 | Offender must be notified
-- src:1791 | (2) Subsection (1) does not apply unless the prosecutor satisfies the court that the offender, before making a plea, was notified that the application of that subsection would be sought.
@ref s 83.27(2) (src:1790-1791)
GIVEN `the prosecutor satisfies the court that the offender, before making a plea, was notified that the application of subsection (1) would be sought` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.27(2) subsection (1) does not apply` MEANS
    IF `the prosecutor satisfies the court that the offender, before making a plea, was notified that the application of subsection (1) would be sought`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "does not apply unless the prosecutor satisfies the court"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

@ref s 83.27(2) (src:1790-1791)
GIVEN `the answer of subsection (1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the prosecutor satisfies the court that the offender, before making a plea, was notified that the application of subsection (1) would be sought` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.27 the person is liable to imprisonment for life, subject to subsection (2)` MEANS
    IF `s 83.27(2) subsection (1) does not apply` `the prosecutor satisfies the court that the offender, before making a plea, was notified that the application of subsection (1) would be sought` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) does not apply unless the prosecutor satisfies the court"
    ELSE `the answer of subsection (1)`
